                <pb facs="0369" n="271" xml:id="pg271"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/5342: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-07-30T15:00:00+08:00">July 30, 1930—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 30—5:58 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>634. Legation’s 605, July 22, 2 p.m.<anchor n="89" xml:id="d333-f1"/> Following
                    from American Consul at Chefoo: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“July 29, 4 p.m. Commissioner of Customs informed me this afternoon Liu
                            Chen-nien is desirous of taking over local customhouse on his own
                            account but was informed that such action might: <list>
                                <item>First, raise international complications;</item>
                                <item>Second, local customs staff including Commissioner would walk
                                    out;</item>
                                <item>Third, difficulty with coast lights;</item>
                                <item>Fourth, difficulty with consuls and fact that there would be
                                    difficulty of carrying on because there is no one to replace
                                    present employees.”</item>
                            </list></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
